class:: QuadratureFeedbackOsc
summary:: Four-output regulated nonlinear rotating system
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

QuadratureFeedbackOsc integrates a two-state Hopf-style rotating system and
returns its four signed directions. Nonlinear feedback distorts the orbit,
external input can push it, and radial regulation attracts it toward unit
radius. RK4 integration runs inside a filtered initialization-rate oversampling
factor.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/SinOsc::. With no feedback it behaves
as a regulated quadrature oscillator; unlike SinOsc it accepts nonlinear
state feedback and external injection.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Signed natural rotation frequency in hertz.

argument:: input
External audio signal.

argument:: feedback
Exactly four feedback values corresponding to x, y, -x, and -y. Each is
clamped to code::-8..8::.

argument:: inject
External-input amount in the x feedback path, clamped to code::-8..8::.

argument:: stability
Radial regulation strength, clamped to code::0..16::.

argument:: drive
Soft-saturation drive for feedback paths, clamped to code::0..16::.

argument:: oversample
Initialization-rate factor code::1::, code::2::, code::4::, or code::8::.

argument:: mul
Multiplier applied to all four outputs.

argument:: add
Offset added to all four outputs after multiplication.

returns::
Four sample-coherent signals in the order x, y, -x, -y.

method:: kr

QuadratureFeedbackOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

Normal outputs are not clipped. A safety limiter rescales the internal state
only if radius exceeds four, and nonfinite state returns to code::[1, 0]::.
Because the last two outputs are generated from the filtered first two, their
sign relations are exact.

examples::

code::
(
{ Splay.ar(QuadratureFeedbackOsc.ar(90)) * 0.045 }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
    var feedback = LFNoise1.kr(
        [0.11, 0.13, 0.17, 0.19]
    ).range(-1.3, 1.3);
    Splay.ar(
        QuadratureFeedbackOsc.ar(
            57, Saw.ar(31, 0.08), feedback,
            inject: 0.6, stability: 1.8,
            drive: 3.5, oversample: 8
        )
    ) * 0.035;
}.play;
)
::

